  "frontier_coordinate": "R-123 reconstructs the fixed R-120 six-row map from A1 and, for the fully assembled contraction-closed conditional endpoint Phi with once-owned trace Theta, reduces the low-chaos data to Lambda=Theta-||Phi-E_0Phi||^2, D0=E_0Lambda, and D1=E_0[xi Lambda]. The direct complete packet has expectation (||E_0Phi||^2-D0)/2, so the R-093 expected-action route needs one aggregate upper bound for D0-||b||^2 rather than D1=0. A source/sextic allocation below 9/20 and 3/20 transfers through the directed chart infimum without a chart-count factor. A bounded full-six-row fixture, a legal first-row theorem, a scalar trace audit, a raw-current Hessian counterexample, and a correlation/frequency boundary sharply delimit shortcuts. The live successor is the stationary-subtracted owner-complete rational/Cartan/R-063 forest trace-excess estimate, uniform in cutoff, chart, control, visits, and representation-preserving refinement. R-121, R-120, R-118, R-103 REG, and R-087/R-093 CORE retain their owners. OVERLAP_src, Nelson, removals, interacting measure, and Sector A remain open.",
